Is cloud-based or on-premises review software better for enterprise deployments?
Cloud-based consumer ratings and reviews software holds a dominant 68.5% market share in 2025 and is the preferred choice for the majority of enterprises due to its lower total cost of ownership, automatic updates, seamless API integrations, and scalability across global markets. On-premises solutions, which account for the remaining 31.5%, are preferred by large enterprises in highly regulated sectors such as healthcare, BFSI, and government where data sovereignty, security compliance frameworks (HIPAA, SOC 2, PCI-DSS), and legacy system integration are critical. Hybrid deployment models are increasingly available from vendors such as Bazaarvoice and PowerReviews, offering cloud-like operational flexibility combined with localized data storage, effectively bridging the gap for security-conscious enterprises. By 2034, the Cloud segment is expected to grow to approximately 80% of the market as private cloud and hybrid architectures satisfy even the most stringent compliance requirements.

Consumer Ratings & Reviews Software Market Analysis by End-User
The E-commerce segment is the dominant end-user vertical in the consumer ratings & reviews software market, reflecting the fundamental role of product reviews in online purchase decision-making. E-commerce businesses, ranging from global marketplace operators and D2C brands to specialized vertical retailers, represent the single largest buyer category, driven by the well-established correlation between review volume, review quality, and conversion rates. Studies consistently show that e-commerce platforms with robust review management systems achieve conversion rates 15-20% higher than peers without structured review programs. The E-commerce segment is projected to grow at a CAGR of 11.6% from 2026 to 2034, as the ongoing global shift from offline to online retail continues and as social commerce, live commerce, and mobile-first shopping further amplify the influence of peer reviews. Platforms such as Yotpo, Judge.me, and Okendo are purpose-built for e-commerce review management, offering deep integrations with Shopify, Magento, WooCommerce, and Salesforce Commerce Cloud.

The Retail segment encompasses both pure-play physical retailers and omnichannel retailers that operate both physical store networks and digital channels. Retail businesses use review and ratings software primarily to manage product reputation across category pages, improve in-store and online product discoverability, and gather structured post-purchase feedback for merchandising and product development decisions. The Retail segment is growing at a CAGR of 9.8% from 2026 to 2034, supported by the ongoing digital transformation of traditional retail chains. The Hospitality segment is one of the highest-growth verticals, expanding at a CAGR of 12.4%, as hotels, restaurants, and travel businesses rely on platforms like TrustYou (travel sector specialist), TripAdvisor-integrated tools, and BirdEye to manage their online reputation across 50+ review platforms simultaneously. The Healthcare vertical is an increasingly significant end-user category, driven by the growth of patient experience management as a regulated quality metric under CMS star ratings programs in the United States and equivalent frameworks globally; the Healthcare segment is growing at a CAGR of 13.2%, the fastest among all end-user categories in this market. BFSI (banking, financial services, and insurance) organizations use review software primarily for branch-level reputation management, financial advisor rating collection, and compliance-aligned testimonial gathering; this segment grows at approximately 9.1% CAGR. The Others category, encompassing automotive, education, professional services, and technology sectors, collectively accounts for approximately 14.2% of market revenue and is growing steadily, with the education sector showing particular momentum following the surge in online learning platform reviews during and after the pandemic.

Which industries are the largest users of consumer ratings and reviews software?
E-commerce is the largest end-user segment of consumer ratings & reviews software, reflecting the foundational role of product reviews in online purchase conversion, followed closely by Retail and Hospitality. Healthcare is emerging as the fastest-growing vertical at a CAGR of 13.2% from 2026 to 2034, driven by CMS patient experience rating requirements, the growth of telehealth platforms, and increasing consumer use of doctor and hospital review sites when selecting healthcare providers. The Hospitality segment, growing at 12.4% CAGR, leverages review platforms to manage reputation across TripAdvisor, Google, Booking.com, and Yelp simultaneously. BFSI institutions use review and ratings tools to manage thousands of branch and advisor-level ratings, ensuring compliance with financial promotion regulations while actively building digital trust scores that influence consumer acquisition and retention. Collectively, these five verticals plus Others represent a diverse and resilient demand base that insulates the consumer ratings & reviews software market from sector-specific cyclicality.

